  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of NNN non-negative integers.\n\nIn one move, you can do the following:\n\n\nchoose (L,R)(L, R)(L,R) such that 1≤L≤R≤∣A∣1 \\le L \\le R \\le |A|1≤L≤R≤∣A∣.\nLet X=MEX†([AL,AL+1,…,AR])X = \\text{MEX}^{\\dagger}([A_L, A_{L + 1}, \\ldots, A_R])X=MEX†([AL​,AL+1​,…,AR​]).\nInsert XXX into the array AAA in any position (possibly at the start or end).\nGiven an integer KKK, find the minimum moves needed to insert KKK into the array. Note that you need to do this even if the array already contains KKK.\n\n†MEX(A)^{\\dagger} \\text{MEX}(A)†MEX(A) denotes the smallest non-negative integer not present in AAA.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains 222 integers - NNN and KKK.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum moves needed to insert KKK into the array.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤K≤N1 \\le K \\le N1≤K≤N",
      "0≤Ai≤N0 \\le A_i \\le N0≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
